tion and separate acceptance criteria. F13 insentient-aware-anole passed without a plan change. Both attestations are signed.","timestamp":1787419598143391001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"F12 passed plan review after four description remediations, but execution preflight found that its seven-path file impact omitted source, generated, parser, and test edits named by the remediated plan. Corrected it to 35 planned paths and expanded its focused verification commands. The prior attestation is stale and must be renewed before claim. F08A remains review-blocked until F12 closes. F08B and F09 certification continues independently.","timestamp":1787423255451842001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Updated the clean implementation worktree to origin/main commit 53eaea07aa2fc5baf5898ff2c279ec348b7601fa. F12, F08B, F09, F10, F13, F19A, F19B, F19C, F19, and F20 hold current certified plan reviews. F08A remains review-blocked until F12 closes. Replaced the epic impact with the 55-path descendant union and recorded 18 deduplicated verification commands. The epic passed non-forced review with zero blockers and was claimed with the configured default assignee.","timestamp":1787427889034195001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress checkpoint for 2026-08-22\n\nUpdated the implementation worktree to `origin/main` at `8a036765705f5ef0e7db4fa21e0926e51d15bafd`.\n\nF20 `aimless-seclusive-tigershark` is closed. GitHub returned the approved About description at `2026-08-22T20:11:28Z` under principal `JoeOakhartNava`. The homepage URL remains empty, and repository topics remain unset. The renewed plan review passed with no blockers. Concurrent tracker writes prevented the first signature write, so the documented `sign-review` recovery persisted the attestation without another model run. Completion verification then passed and closed the ticket without force.\n\nRead-only implementation contracts are complete for the next independent shards.\n\n- F08B covers README Git requirements, declared dependency floors, and provider extras.\n- F09 corrects README and internal documentation from legacy HMAC descriptions to the current DSSE, SSHSIG, and Ed25519 operation-certificate model while preserving the retained generic HMAC utilities.\n- F19A corrects generated configuration exposure language to describe the CLI surface without claiming an MCP configuration tool.\n- F19B adds field-owned public descriptions to the generated configuration reference and extracts `VerifyConfig` to `src/rebar/_config_schema_verify.py` while preserving public import identity.\n- F19C corrects ADR links and the active shadow-composition behavior in `docs/config.md`. The matching stale text in `docs/reuse-surface.md` remains outside F19C and requires a separately authorized ticket or explicit scope expansion.\n\nF12 remains the first implementation dependency for F08A and F10. F13 and the README and configuration shards remain independent of F12.","timestamp":1787431546078322001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"F13 implementation started in /Users/joeoakhart/docs-f13-mcp. Worktree refreshed and clean at origin/main 7825673f8679b4ac2785c6865fe28afd252e7f6b. Plan review remained certified, so no renewal was required. Claimed insentient-aware-anole without force as joeoakhart@navapbc.com. Beginning a test-first cycle for complete first-paragraph MCP summaries, later-paragraph exclusion, Markdown pipe escaping, and the transition_ticket description correction.","timestamp":1787437050924187001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"F13 insentient-aware-anole TDD cycle 1: RED proved missing compl